  "description": "A copy of the r-fmt-2b-w-accdb fixture (123 pages; page 122, Au4's old data page, is the only free page inside the file). Au1: tdef 107, usage maps 108, PK root 109, ten rows (IDs 1-10, 21-23 bytes) on data page 110. Pg: tdef 52, usage maps 53 (owned {55, 56, 57}, FreeMap {57}), PK root 54, 12 rows of ID and eight Text(255) fields of 61 U+20AC (1004 bytes each); rows 1-4 fill page 55 with 58 bytes free. One session runs UPDATE Pg SET T1 = 255 U+20AC, T2 = 255 U+20AC, T3 = 255 U+20AC, T4 = 255 U+20AC, T5 = 73 U+20AC WHERE ID = 2 (row 2 grows from 1004 to 2580 bytes) and closes. The grown row moves to free page 122 (FreeMap page 57 has no room), which is left with 1500 bytes free. Asks whether page 122 joins Pg's FreeMap (slot 1 of page 53): 1,057 bytes free stayed out (r-cplx-rebuild create-rb-rich-accdb), 2,956 and 3,016 joined (r-q16). Each session opens the database shared read/write through DAO, runs its statements with dbFailOnError (RecordsAffected read), and closes, with the DBEngine alive. Each read keeps page 0 bytes 3584-3591 and pages 1, 53, 55, 122; after Close every page's hash too.",
